Hi @{{ author }}, thank you for the report.

This issue looks like a model download problem. Most of these are fixed with a clean download. Please do these steps before we investigate:

1. Update mflux to the latest release.
2. Make sure the disk has enough free space. Large models need tens of GB.
3. If the model is gated on Hugging Face (for example FLUX.1-dev), accept the license on the model page. Then log in: `hf auth login`.
4. Delete the partial or corrupt download. The cache folder is `~/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--<org>--<name>`. If you use `HF_HOME`, look there.
5. Download the model again: `hf download <org>/<name>`. You can also run your `mflux-generate` command again. It downloads the model on first use.
6. Run your original command again.

If the same error occurs after a clean download, please reply with:

- The full command you ran.
- The full error output.
- The output of `pip show mflux` (or `uv tool list`).
- The macOS version and the amount of RAM.

We will then look at the issue. This comment was posted by an automated triage action. A maintainer will review the issue if the steps above do not help.
